sequenceDiagram
    participant vLLM as vLLM Engine<br/>(GPU Node)
    participant CE as LMCache Engine<br/>(initiator, alt track)
    participant SM as StorageManager
    participant L1 as LocalCPUBackend<br/>(L1 DRAM)
    participant TX as WAL / COW map<br/>(initiator-side)
    participant RB as RawBlockL2Adapter<br/>(io_uring / O_DIRECT)
    participant K as Kernel NVMe-oF<br/>(nvmet-rdma)
    participant JBOF as NVMe JBOF<br/>(remote namespace)
    participant GPU as GPU Connector<br/>(DMA to HBM)

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: Initiator-owned + remote-NVMe-oF-L2 alt track.<br/>Storage node runs no LMCache agent — only nvmet-rdma exports namespaces.<br/>Semantic admission, key→LBA map, integrity metadata, and durable-commit ordering all live on the initiator.

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: === RETRIEVE (Cache Lookup) ===

    vLLM->>CE: retrieve(tokens)
    CE->>CE: TokenDatabase: hash tokens → chunk keys (BLAKE3)
    CE->>SM: batched_contains(keys)
    SM->>L1: batched_contains(keys)

    alt L1 HIT (page in DRAM)
        L1-->>SM: hit_chunks = N
        SM-->>CE: block_mapping: {LocalCPUBackend: keys}
        CE->>L1: get(keys)
        L1-->>CE: MemoryObj (pinned DRAM buffer)
        CE->>GPU: load → DMA to GPU HBM
        GPU-->>vLLM: KV in HBM, resume inference
    else L1 MISS → check L2 map
        L1-->>SM: hit_chunks = 0
        SM->>TX: lookup(keys) → LBA extents + checksum ref
        alt L2 HIT (key present in initiator map)
            TX-->>SM: LBAs + checksum refs
            SM->>RB: submit_load_task(LBAs, dst_buffers)
            RB->>K: io_uring submit (O_DIRECT read, 256KB)
            K->>JBOF: NVMe Read Command (nvmet-rdma)
            JBOF-->>K: NVMe Read Response (256KB)
            K-->>RB: completion → data in registered DRAM
            RB->>RB: recompute BLAKE3, compare to checksum ref
            alt VALIDATE OK
                RB-->>CE: load complete
                CE->>L1: promote to L1 (optional)
                CE->>GPU: load → DMA to GPU HBM
                GPU-->>vLLM: KV in HBM, resume inference
            else VALIDATE FAIL
                RB->>TX: mark key stale / discard map entry
                RB-->>CE: load failed (integrity)
                CE-->>vLLM: miss (recompute)
            end
        else L2 MISS (no map entry)
            TX-->>SM: not present
            SM-->>CE: total_hit_chunks = 0
            CE-->>vLLM: miss mask (recompute these tokens)
        end
    end

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: === STORE (After KV Computation) — durable commit ===

    vLLM->>CE: store(tokens, kv_tensors)
    CE->>GPU: GPU HBM → DMA to host DRAM
    CE->>CE: hash tokens → chunk keys, compute per-page BLAKE3 digest D
    CE->>SM: put(keys, memory_objs, digests)
    SM->>L1: put(keys, data) → pinned in DRAM (L1)

    Note over SM,TX: Initiator-side durable commit begins here.<br/>Order of the four steps below is what makes the commit crash-safe.

    SM->>TX: 1. append intent { key, LBA_range, D } to WAL (or reserve new COW generation)
    TX->>K: fsync/FLUSH intent log
    K->>JBOF: NVMe FLUSH → durable

    SM->>RB: 2. submit_store_task(LBA_range, data, FUA)
    RB->>K: io_uring submit (O_DIRECT write with FUA, 256KB)
    K->>JBOF: NVMe Write (FUA) → durable payload
    JBOF-->>K: completion
    K-->>RB: completion

    RB->>TX: 3. write checksum record (D, LBA_range) with FUA
    TX->>K: io_uring submit (checksum write with FUA)
    K->>JBOF: NVMe Write (FUA) → durable checksum
    JBOF-->>K: completion

    TX->>TX: 4. publish key→LBA map atomically<br/>(WAL commit record OR COW generation-pointer flip)
    TX->>K: fsync/FLUSH map publication
    K->>JBOF: NVMe FLUSH → durable
    TX-->>SM: store ACK (terminal, cache-visible)

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: === RECOVERY (restart / nvme reconnect) ===

    CE->>TX: replay WAL (or read active COW generation)
    TX->>K: read intent log + checksum region
    K->>JBOF: NVMe Reads (nvmet-rdma)
    JBOF-->>K: log + checksum blocks
    K-->>TX: bytes
    TX->>TX: reconstruct key-to-LBA map from committed WAL records only<br/>uncommitted intents become GC candidates<br/>committed records with missing or bad checksum are discarded<br/>unreferenced blocks are freed on next GC pass
    TX-->>CE: map ready
    CE-->>vLLM: cache online

    Note over vLLM,JBOF: === GARBAGE COLLECTION (background) ===

    TX->>TX: scan WAL / COW generations, identify orphan LBA ranges
    TX->>RB: release_slots(LBA_range)
    RB->>K: io_uring TRIM/UNMAP (optional)
    K->>JBOF: NVMe Dataset Management → deallocate
